\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The Galilean fishers toil
\par All night and nothing take;
\par But Jesus comes-a wondrous spoil\tab 
\par Is lifted from the lake.
\par Lord, when our neigbours are in vain
\par And vain the help of men,
\par When fruitless is our care and pain
\par Come, blessed Jesus, then!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The night is dark, the surges fill
\par The bark, the wild winds roar;
\par But Jesus comes; and all in still-
\par The ship is at the shore.
\par O Lord, when storms around howl,
\par And all is dark and dear,
\par In all the tempests of the soul,
\par O blessed Jesus, hear!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. A frail one, thrice denying Thee,
\par Saw mercy in Thine eyes;
\par The penitent upon the three
\par Was borne to Paradise.
\par In hours of sin and deep distress
\par O show us, Lord, Thy face;
\par In penitential loneliness,
\par O give us, Jesus, grace!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The faithful full retire in fear,
\par To their closed upper room;
\par But, suddenly, with joyful cheer
\par They see their Master come.
\par Lord, come to us, unloose our bands,
\par And bid our terrors cease;
\par Lift over us Thy blessed hands,
\par Speak, holy Jesus, peace!
\par Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

